+### 1.4 Denominator increments `A_2,A_1`
+
+Because the only preceding radius for `delta_2` is the integral `delta_3`,
+`A_2` is the reduced denominator of `delta_2`.  With `L=8a+5`, its raw
+numerator and denominator are
+
+```text
+2(3L-1)=4(12a+7),
+3(5L-1)=4*6(5a+3).
