which equals `J/g_y` because `J[y,x+y^k]=-1`; interpolation recovers `y`.
The exponents of `1/g_y` are `-(k-1)/k-j`, `j>=0`, so none is `-1`.

For the target-independent negative control

```text
g=y^2-x^2-x,
```

the two roots give

```text
1/g_y(tau_+)= +(1/2)t + ...,
1/g_y(tau_-) =-(1/2)t + ... .
